## 🆕 Feature #1: Tour Side Panel

### **Before (v6.1):**
- Center modal that blocks the prototype
- User must close to interact
- Can't reference instructions while testing

### **After (v6.2):**
- **Left-side panel** that stays open
- User can interact with prototype **while reading**
- Minimize button collapses to small tab
- Progress dots show tour position
- Much better for user research!

### **Tour Panel Features:**
```
┌────────────────────────────────┐
│ Step 3 of 8          [–] [×]  │
│                                │
│ Token-Based Verification       │
│                                │
│ Description text here...       │
│                                │
│ ✓ Try this:                    │
│ • Click Verify Now             │
│ • Review cost modal            │
│ • Notice token deduction       │
│                                │
│ 💡 Tip: You can interact with  │
│ the prototype while this panel │
│ is open. Try clicking →        │
│                                │
│ [← Previous]     [Next →]      │
│                                │
│ ● ● ● ○ ○ ○ ○ ○  (progress)   │
└────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Panel Controls:**
- **Minimize (–)**: Collapses to small left-edge tab
- **Close (×)**: Ends tour completely
- **Previous/Next**: Navigate tour steps
- **Progress Dots**: Visual tour position

**Key Benefits:**
- ✅ Users can read AND interact simultaneously
- ✅ No need to memorize instructions
- ✅ Natural workflow testing
- ✅ Less facilitator intervention needed

